The attached image (Fig. 6 from the npj Vaccines paper) demonstrates Nano-11's ability to improve antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells and increase antigen retention at the injection site. Panel a shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of the costimulatory molecule CD86 among OVA-positive cells in draining lymph nodes. Panel b further characterizes OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs by CD11b and Ly6C expression. Panel c uses in vivo imaging to illustrate that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) formulated with Nano-11 (OVA+N11) or aluminum hydroxide (OVA+AH) is retained at the injection site for a significantly longer period (up to day 7) compared to soluble OVA alone, which rapidly clears by day 2.